.\"
.\" Tcl/Tk Macro definitions - borrowed from Tcl/Tk man pages.
.\"     # Set up traps and other miscellaneous stuff for Tcl/Tk man pages.
.if t .wh -1.3i ^B
.nr ^l \n(.l
.ad b
'\" .BS Start box enclosure.  From here until next .BE, everything will be
'\"     enclosed in one large box.
.de BS
.br
.mk ^y
.nr ^b 1u
.if n .nf
.if n .ti 0
.if n \l'\\n(.lu\(ul'
.if n .fi
..
./"
'\" .BE End of box enclosure.
.de BE
.nf
.ti 0
.mk ^t
.ie n \l'\\n(^lu\(ul'
.el \{\
.\"     Draw four-sided box normally, but don't draw top of
.\"     box if the box started on an earlier page.
.ie !\\n(^b-1 \{\
\h'-1.5n'\L'|\\n(^yu-1v'\l'\\n(^lu+3n\(ul'\L'\\n(^tu+1v-\\n(^yu'\l'|0u-1.5n\(ul'
.\}
.el \}\
\h'-1.5n'\L'|\\n(^yu-1v'\h'\\n(^lu+3n'\L'\\n(^tu+1v-\\n(^yu'\l'|0u-1.5n\(ul'
.\}
.\}
.fi
.br
.nr ^b 0
..
./"
'\" .CS Begin code excerpt.
.de CS
.RS
.nf
.ta .25i .5i .75i 1i
..
./"
'\" .CE End code excerpt.
.de CE
.fi
.RE
..
./"
'\" .DS Begin an indented unfilled display.
.de DS
.RS
.nf
.sp
..
./"
'\" .DE End of indented unfilled display.
'\"
.de DE
.fi
.RE
.sp
..
./"
'\" .OP cmdName dbName dbClass
'\"     Start of description of a specific option.  cmdName gives the
'\"     option's name as specified in the class command, dbName gives
'\"     the option's name in the option database, and dbClass gives
'\"     the option's class in the option database.
.de OP
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c
Command-Line Name:      \\fB\\$1\\fR
Database Name:  \\fB\\$2\\fR
Database Class: \\fB\\$3\\fR
.fi
.IP
..
./"
'\" .SO Start of list of standard options for a Tk widget.  The
'\"     options follow on successive lines, in four columns separated
'\"     by tabs.
.de SO
.SH "STANDARD OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
.ft B
..
./"
'\" .SE End of list of standard options for a Tk widget.
'\"     Start of description of a specific option.  cmdName gives the
'\"     option's name as specified in the class command, dbName gives
'\"     the option's name in the option database, and dbClass gives
'\"     the option's class in the option database.
.de SE
.fi
.ft R
.LP
See the \\fBoptions\\fR manual entry for details on the standard options.
..
.\"
.\"**********************************************************************
.\"				End of Macros!!!
.\"**********************************************************************
.TH CLed n 03/08/98 "CADC"
.\".BS
.SH NAME
CLed \- Create and manipulate a LED widget.

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBCLed\fI \fIpathName \fR?\fIoptions\fR?

.SH "INHERITANCE"
itk::Widget \<- CLed

.SO
\-background		\-cursor
.SE

.SH "INHERITED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-clientdata\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBitk::Widget\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited options.

.SH "WIDGET-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"

.OP \-colorassoc colorAssociation ColorAssociation
List that associates a color with a value.  The value of the 
variable specified by the -ledvariable option is used to 
determine the color of the LED.  The list should be something
like:
.IP
{{green good} {yellow warning} {red bad}}.
.IP
Note that a case insensitive match is used between the variable's
value and the color association list.

.OP \-led led Led
Specifies whether the LED is "on" or "off"  Default is value
is "off".  This is a boolean value and accepts any of the
values accepted by \fBTcl_GetBoolean\fR, as well as \fIbusy\fR,
and \fIidle\fR.  The default value is "off".

.OP \-ledcolor ledColor Background
Specifies the color of the LED. The default color is grey85.


.OP \-ledmargin ledMargin Margin
Specifies the margin between the LED and the  childsite
in any of the forms acceptable to \fBTK_GetPixels\fR.
The default is one pixel.

.OP \-ledpos ledPos Position
Specifies the relative position of the LED with respect
to the childsite: n, ne, e, se, s, sw, w, or nw. The
default is w.

.OP \-ledvariable ledVariable Variable
Specifies a variable whose value is to be monitored, The
value of this variable determines the color of the LED.

.OP \-ledwidth ledWidth Width
Specifies the width of the LED.

.OP \-offcolor offColor Background
Specifies the color of the LED when it is off.  The default value is
grey.

.OP \-oncolor onColor Background
Specifies the color of the LED when it is on. The default value is
green.
.\".BE

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBCLed\fR command creates a new window (given by the
\fIpathName\fR argument) and makes it into a LED widget.
Additional options, described above, may be specified on the 
command line or in the option database to configure aspects of
the LED. The \fBCLed\fR command returns its
\fIpathName\fR argument.  At the time this command is invoked,
there must not exist a window named \fIpathName\fR, but
\fIpathName\fR's parent must exist.

.SH "WIDGET COMMAND"
The \fBCLed\fR command creates a new Tcl command whose
name is \fIpathName\fR.  This
command may be used to invoke various
operations on the widget.  It has the following general form:
.CS
\fIpathName method \fR?\fIarg arg ...\fR?
.CE
\fImethod\fR and the \fIarg\fRs
determine the exact behavior of the command.  
.PP
The following methods are possible for LED widgets:
.TP
\fIpathName \fBalignleds\fR  \fIwidget\fR ?\fIwidget ...\fR?
This method aligns a list of widgets derived from the CLed class.
It adjusts the LED margins so that each of the widgets has the
same total space for the combination of LED and margin.  The
net effect is to left align the LEDs.  Generally, this method
is only useful with the LEDs in the "w" position, which is 
the default.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcget\fR \fIoption\fR
Returns the current value of the configuration option given
by \fIoption\fR.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCLed\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBchildsite\fR
Return the path name of the child site.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcomponent\fR ?\fIname\fR? ?\fIcommand arg arg ...\fR?
Used to query or access component widgets within the LED
widget.  With no arguments, this returns a list of
symbolic names for component widgets that are accessible in the
current scope.  
.sp
If a symbolic \fIname\fR is specified this method returns the window
path name for that component.
.sp
Otherwise, the \fIcommand\fR and any remaining \fIarg\fR arguments
are invoked as a method on the component with the symbolic \fIname\fR.
This provides a well-defined mechanism for accessing internal components
without relying on specific window path names.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBconfig\fR
See \fBconfigure\fI.

.TP
\fIpathName\fR \fBconfigure\fR ?\fIoption\fR? ?\fIvalue option value ...\fR?
Query or modify the configuration options of the widget.
If no \fIoption\fR is specified, returns a list describing all of
the available options for \fIpathName\fR (see \fBTk_ConfigureInfo\fR for
information on the format of this list).  If \fIoption\fR is specified
with no \fIvalue\fR, then the command returns a list describing the
one named option (this list will be identical to the corresponding
sublist of the value returned if no \fIoption\fR is specified).  If
one or more \fIoption\-value\fR pairs are specified, then the command
modifies the given widget option(s) to have the given value(s);  in
this case the command returns an empty string.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCLed\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBisa\fR \fBclassName\fR
Sets the LED widget's class to the specified class name.

.SH "COMPONENTS"
.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBled\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
This component is the "led" of the led widget. See the 
\fBframe\fR widget manual
entry for details on the lwchildsite component item.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBledmargin\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
This component provides control over the spacing 
between the led and lwchildsite component. 
See the \fBframe\fR widget manual
entry for details on the lwchildsite component item.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBlwchildsite\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
The lwchildsite component is the user child site for
the led widget.  See the \fBframe\fR widget manual
entry for details on the lwchildsite component item.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBshell\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
This component is the outer shell, widget, of the led
widget.
See the \fBframe\fR widget manual
entry for details on the lwchildsite component item.

.SH "DEFAULT BINDINGS"
.PP
No bindings are defined for this widget except those defined for the
various components this widget is comprised of.
.PP
See the \fBFrame\fR manual entries for more information.
pages for more information.

.SH EXAMPLE
.DS
 CLed .led -ledcolor green 
 set childsite [ .led childsite ]
 label $childsite.label -text "Command Server"

 pack .led  -fill both -expand yes
.DE

.SH AUTHOR
Shannon Jaeger

.SH KEYWORDS
LED, widget
